<title>JAPAN: Germany's KFW launches yen/US$ dual samurai bond.</title>
<headline>Germany's KFW launches yen/US$ dual samurai bond.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/U.S. dollar dual samurai issue was announced by lead-manager Yamaichi Securities on Wednesday.</p>
<p>BORROWER Kreditanstalt fur Wiederaufbau</p>
<p>    AMT	30 bln yen</p>
<p>    COUPON   5.4 pct</p>
<p>MATURITY 19 May 2000</p>
<p>TYPE dual samuraiISS PRICE par  PAY DATE 20 May 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	May 1-19</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA   Moody's Aaa</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Yamaichi Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Fuji Bank</p>
<p>NOTES: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive $3,957.26 for each 500,000 yen bond held until maturity.</p>
<p>---Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3748</p>
</text>
